  <div class="section-container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Why Self-Employed Face Tax Problems</h2>
    <div class="service-content-full">
      <p>When you're self-employed, you're responsible for both the employer and employee portions of Social Security and Medicare taxes—that's 15.3% right off the top, before income tax. Add inconsistent income, unexpected expenses, and the complexity of quarterly estimated payments, and it's easy to see how tax debt accumulates.</p>
      <p>The good news? An IRS Installment Agreement lets you pay your tax debt in monthly payments over time. It's the most common way to resolve tax debt, and it's much easier to qualify for than an Offer in Compromise.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

